#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:5
msgid "A *working schedule* defines the hours employees are expected to work. It is set on the employee's :doc:`contract <contracts>` and on the employee record, and it is the reference against which :doc:`attendances <../attendances>` and :doc:`time off <../time_off>` are measured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:9
msgid "To see the configured working schedules, go to :menuselection:`Employees app --> Configuration --> Working Schedules`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:12
msgid "Working schedules are company-specific. In a multi-company database, every company needs its own schedules; the :guilabel:`Company` column only appears when more than one company exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:16
msgid "A database with five companies that all work a standard 40-hour week needs five separate 40-hour working schedules, one per company."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:30
msgid "Create a working schedule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:32
msgid "Click :guilabel:`New` and fill in the form. The form has a general information section and a :guilabel:`Working Hours` tab listing the individual time ranges per day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:35
msgid ":guilabel:`Name`: a descriptive name, such as `Standard 20 Hours/Week`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:36
msgid ":guilabel:`Company`: the company the schedule belongs to. An empty field makes it available to all companies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:38
msgid ":guilabel:`Timezone`: the time zone the hours are expressed in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:39
msgid ":guilabel:`Flexible Hours`: tick this checkbox when employees may work their hours freely rather than at fixed times. The :guilabel:`Working Hours` tab then disappears, the :guilabel:`Company Full Time` field is relabeled :guilabel:`Hours per Week`, and :guilabel:`Average Hour per Day` becomes editable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:43
msgid ":guilabel:`Company Full Time`: the number of hours per week that counts as full time in the company, typically `40`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:45
msgid ":guilabel:`Average Hour per Day`: computed from the :guilabel:`Working Hours` tab, and editable on a flexible schedule. It is used wherever a day has to be converted into hours, for example when a day of time off is deducted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:49
msgid "Next, configure the :guilabel:`Working Hours` tab. Each line has a :guilabel:`Day of Week`, a :guilabel:`Day Period` (:guilabel:`Morning`, :guilabel:`Lunch`, or :guilabel:`Afternoon`), and a :guilabel:`Work from` and :guilabel:`Work to` time. A default 40-hour week is pre-filled with morning (8:00-12:00), lunch (12:00-13:00), and afternoon (13:00-17:00) lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:55
msgid ":guilabel:`Work from` and :guilabel:`Work to` use the 24-hour format: `2:00 PM` is entered as `14:00`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:59
msgid "If the hours alternate between two weeks, click :guilabel:`Switch to 2 weeks calendar` at the top of the form. The :guilabel:`Working Hours` tab then shows an even and an odd week that can be configured separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:72
msgid "Working schedules cannot be shared between companies. Each company needs its own set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/employees/working_schedules.rst:74
msgid "The company's default schedule for new employees is selected as :guilabel:`Company Working Hours` in :menuselection:`Employees app --> Configuration --> Settings`."
msgstr ""

