msgid ":guilabel:`Sign-off`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:81
msgid "The sign-off state, the timestamps and the employee's own comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:93
msgid "A row of smart buttons sits above them: :guilabel:`My Answers` opens the part of the questionnaire you personally have to fill in, :guilabel:`Objectives` the employee's objectives, :guilabel:`Development Actions` the plan, :guilabel:`Meeting` the review conversation once one has been scheduled, and :guilabel:`Review History` this employee's other reviews."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:101
msgid "Opening the review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:103
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Open the Review`. This is the moment the review becomes real, and a great deal is fixed in place:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:106
msgid "the **reviewers** are snapshotted from the employee's management line, together with the **department** and the **job position**. If the employee moves department in March, the review opened in February still says where they were and who reviewed them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:109
msgid "the **questionnaire version** and the **rating scale** are stamped, so that a new version released next week does not rewrite a review already in progress;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:111
msgid "the **objectives** of the period are pulled in — the ones whose dates overlap the review period;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:113
msgid "the questions each person has to answer are created;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:114
msgid "one to-do is placed on **each participant's** own record — never on the review, so that the employee cannot see who else was asked;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:116
msgid "the unfinished development actions of the previous review are copied in, marked as carried over;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:118
msgid "the opening mail goes out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:120
msgid "Opening is refused, with a message saying which, when the employee has no manager, when no questionnaire can be resolved, when the questionnaire found has not been released, or when no rating scale can be resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:125
msgid "After launching a cycle you have a list of drafts. Select them all in the list view and click :guilabel:`Open the Reviews`. Whatever could not be opened is reported by employee name and reason, and the rest are opened."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:132
msgid "The self-assessment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:134
msgid "The employee gets a mail and a to-do. On their review, they click :guilabel:`Fill in my part` (or the :guilabel:`My Answers` smart button) and answer the questions addressed to them. Answers save as they are entered; nothing is submitted until they say so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:138
msgid "When they are ready, they click :guilabel:`Submit my Self-Assessment`. If a required question is still unanswered, the submission is refused and the missing questions are named."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:141
msgid "Submitting freezes those answers. From then on the employee can still read them but no longer change them; only an HR officer can correct a submitted answer, and it is recorded that they did."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:146
msgid ":guilabel:`Self-Assessment Progress` on the review shows how much of the required part is answered, so a reviewer can see whether it is worth chasing without reading anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:152
msgid "The manager assessment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:154
msgid "The reviewer answers their own part the same way, and additionally sets the **proposed rating** on the :guilabel:`Rating` page, on the confidential assessment. :guilabel:`Submit the Manager Assessment` is refused without it: a review with no rating is an opinion that was never committed to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:160
msgid "Preparing well"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:162
msgid "Four things on the form exist to make the assessment about facts rather than about the last three weeks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:165
msgid "**The objectives of the period**, with every dated check-in behind them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:166
msgid "**The previous plan**, on the first page: what was agreed last time, and what came of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:167
msgid "**The reviewer's working notes**, on the :guilabel:`Notes` page — what you wrote down in March, when it happened. A note belongs to its author; another reviewer does not see it. Read :doc:`confidentiality` on what a note is and is not before you rely on that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:170
msgid "**The evidence panel.** On the :guilabel:`Evidence` page, :guilabel:`Show the evidence of the period` gathers what was actually recorded about this employee between :guilabel:`From` and :guilabel:`To` from the modules that keep it — today, the check-ins on their objectives. Every entry is resolved with **your own** access rights, so the panel can never show a reviewer something they were not already entitled to read, and it will show an employee looking at their own review a shorter list than it shows their manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:178
msgid "Calibration happens on the confidential assessment, not on the review. If the final rating ends up different from the one the reviewer proposed, both are kept and a written reason is required. Neither the proposal nor the reason is ever shown to the employee. See :doc:`confidentiality`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:186
msgid "The review conversation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:188
msgid "The conversation is the point of the exercise; the record is the residue. :guilabel:`Schedule the Review Conversation` creates a calendar event attached to the review and fills in :guilabel:`Review Meeting`, after which the :guilabel:`Meeting` smart button opens it. The meeting belongs to the review: it is removed with it if the review is cancelled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:193
msgid "Hold the conversation around the release, not after it. An employee who reads their rating in a system before anybody has spoken to them about it has already formed their view of the process by the time the meeting starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:200
msgid "Sharing the review with the employee"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:202
msgid ":guilabel:`Share with the Employee` releases the review. It:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:204
msgid "makes the reviewer's answers visible to the employee — but only for the questions marked :guilabel:`Shared With Employee`, and never an answer given anonymously;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:206
msgid "copies the proposed rating into the final rating if no final rating has been set yet;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:207
msgid "moves the review to :guilabel:`Shared` and mails the employee;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:208
msgid "records on the confidential log who released it, with which final rating, and how many answers were made visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:211
msgid "If the cycle's release mode is *HR releases, then the manager shares*, a reviewer pressing this button is refused: an officer releases centrally. That is how you calibrate a whole cycle before anybody sees a rating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:218
msgid "Sign-off: acknowledged, or disagreed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:220
msgid "Sign-off is **not** a statement that the employee agrees with the review. It is a record that they were shown it, plus room for what they think of it. Both outcomes close the review equally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:223
msgid ":guilabel:`I acknowledge this review` records that the employee has read and accepted it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:224
msgid ":guilabel:`I disagree with this review` opens a short form that asks for their own words, and refuses to record an empty one. A recorded dissent with no words in it would be worth nothing to the employee later, which is exactly when it matters. They write what they disagree with under :guilabel:`My Comment` and click :guilabel:`Record my Comment`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:229
msgid "Either way the review is locked, the moment is timestamped, and the employee's own words are stored on the review, shown on the :guilabel:`Sign-off` page and printed on **every** copy of the review packet, including the reviewer's and HR's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:234
msgid "Only the employee under review can sign off, and only through those two acts. There is no field a manager or an officer can write to say that an employee acknowledged something."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:237
msgid "If an employee is slow, the reviewer can ask again: a sign-off reminder mail goes to the employee without disclosing anything new, since the review is already shared with them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:243
msgid "Closing the review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:245
msgid ":guilabel:`Close the Review` finishes it. It is refused unless the review has been shared, and — when the cycle requires sign-off — unless the employee has signed off. A final rating is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:249
msgid "Closing writes the employee's last review and, if automatic planning is on, their next review date; closes the outstanding to-dos; runs the write-backs of the optional modules (competency levels, for instance); stamps the **retention date**; and locks the review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:256
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:40
msgid "The development plan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:258
msgid "The development plan is what a review is actually for, and it is the part designed to outlive the review that created it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:269
msgid "Add one line per action on the :guilabel:`Development Plan` page: a :guilabel:`Name`, a :guilabel:`Type` (*Training*, *Mentoring*, *Coaching*, *Stretch Assignment*, *Rotation*, *Certification*, *Reading*, *Other*), an :guilabel:`Owner`, a :guilabel:`Deadline`, optionally a :guilabel:`Cost` and a link to an :guilabel:`Objective`. Under :guilabel:`What we agreed`, write what will be done and what good looks like."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:275
msgid "As the action progresses, keep :guilabel:`Status` up to date and fill in :guilabel:`What came of it`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:279
msgid "Carry-forward"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:281
msgid "When the next review of the same employee is opened, every action still *Planned* or *In Progress* is copied onto it and marked as carried over, together with the outcome recorded so far. The next review's first page is therefore *Previous Plan*: what we agreed, and what happened."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:286
msgid "That is the mechanism that stops a development plan from being a promise made once a year and never mentioned again. An action that has been carried forward twice is visible as such, which is a conversation worth having."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:293
msgid "Printing a review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:295
msgid ":guilabel:`Print` produces the review packet: the employee, job, department, cycle and period; the questionnaire with the answers; the released rating; the development plan; the sign-off block with the employee's own comment; and the retention date in the footer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:299
msgid "The same template serves everybody. The employee's copy contains less than the reviewer's, because the document only renders what its reader is entitled to see — the rating block, for example, is only present for a reviewer or an officer. There is no separate \"employee version\" that somebody could forget to keep in step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:307
msgid "Correcting a finished review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:309
msgid "A signed-off review is locked. That lock is real: it is refused through the interface, through an import, and on the answers underneath it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:312
msgid "An HR officer can lift it with :guilabel:`Unlock` or :guilabel:`Reopen`, and either one asks for a :guilabel:`Reason` before it will do anything. The reason goes on the confidential log with their name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:316
msgid ":guilabel:`Unlock` leaves the review closed but makes it writable again, for a correction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:317
msgid ":guilabel:`Reopen` puts a closed review back into the shared state, where the employee is asked for their sign-off once more — the honest option whenever the correction changes something the employee was told."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:321
msgid "Unlocking is refused once the review has reached its retention date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:324
msgid "Cancelling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:326
msgid ":guilabel:`Cancel` is for a review that will not happen. It closes the outstanding to-dos and removes the review meeting. An officer can bring a cancelled review back to draft. A review that has already started cannot be deleted — cancel it instead, so the record of what was planned and dropped survives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:332
msgid ":doc:`confidentiality` — what each party sees at every step above"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:333
msgid ":doc:`objectives` — the objectives and check-ins the assessment reads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:334
msgid ":doc:`multi_rater` — adding peer, direct report and outside feedback to this flow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/conducting_a_review.rst:335
msgid ":doc:`competencies` — the competency page and the write-back that runs at closing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:3
msgid "Confidentiality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:5
msgid "A performance review contains an opinion about a person, written down and kept for years. Who may read which part of it is not a preference to be configured later: it is the first thing to get right, and the reason several parts of this application are laid out the way they are."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:9
msgid "This page is written for the person who has to answer, in a works council meeting or to a data protection authority, the question *\"who can see this?\"*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:15
msgid "Who can see what"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:18
msgid "What"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:18
msgid "Their reviewer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:18
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:136
msgid "HR officer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:20
msgid "The review itself: period, dates, status, who reviews them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:20
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:40
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:42
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:42
msgid "Read"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:20
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:23
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:25
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:40
msgid "Read and write"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:20
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:23
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:25
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:31
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:37
#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/confidentiality.rst:40
