#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:76
msgid "Whether a role is anonymous is decided **per role, per cycle**, and it is a promise. Once raters have answered under it, it is not something to reconsider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:82
msgid "The anonymity threshold, and what it refuses to do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:84
msgid "An anonymous role is pooled: the reviewer and the employee see an average per question and the written remarks shuffled into a random order, never an individual answer and never a name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:87
msgid "Pooling only protects people if there are enough of them. The threshold — :guilabel:`Anonymity Threshold` on the cycle, falling back to :guilabel:`Minimum Answers Before Aggregation` in the company settings — is the number of submitted answers a role must reach before anything at all is released for it. It defaults to 5, and **it cannot be set below 5**, in the settings or anywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:93
msgid "Below the threshold, nothing is shown. Not the average, not the remarks, and **not even how many people answered**. That last one is the part that is usually got wrong elsewhere: a count on its own is enough to identify a small group across rounds. If two peers answered this year and three last year, and you know who left, you can work out who said what."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:99
msgid "Refused at launch, not at release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:101
msgid "If an anonymous role could never gather enough answers, the **launch is refused**. Not the release — the launch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:104
msgid "That timing is the whole point. Refusing at release time would mean the round ran, people answered under a promise of anonymity, and only afterwards did anybody discover the promise could not be kept. By then the only options are to break the promise or to throw the answers away, and both are bad."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:109
msgid "Three situations are refused, each naming the cycle and the role:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:111
msgid "the round promises anonymity to a role but asks for **fewer** raters of that role than the threshold, so it could never release anything;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:113
msgid "the round promises anonymity but **caps** that role below the threshold;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:114
msgid "some employees in scope simply **do not have** enough possible raters of that role — a team of three cannot produce five peers. The message names how many employees are affected and how many raters each of them actually has."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:118
msgid "In each case the fix is one of three: take those employees out of scope, turn the anonymity of that role off for this round, or leave the round unlaunched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:122
msgid "The same check runs again when a panel is approved and when an employee nominates, so an anonymous role that has been whittled down to four people by rejections is caught before anybody is invited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:129
msgid "Nomination and approval"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:131
msgid "The reviewer starts the nomination round with :guilabel:`Ask for Nominations`. The employee is mailed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:133
msgid "The employee opens their review and clicks :guilabel:`Propose my Raters`. The form asks for :guilabel:`Peers`, :guilabel:`Direct Reports`, :guilabel:`Skip Levels` and :guilabel:`Outside Contacts` (one per line, as ``Anna Nagy <anna.nagy@example.com>`` or just the address), plus a :guilabel:`Message to the reviewer` explaining the choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:137
msgid "The employee submits. The reviewer is mailed and finds the proposals waiting on the :guilabel:`Participants` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:139
msgid "The reviewer accepts each nomination, turns it down, or replaces it with somebody else — which keeps the trace of both, and asks for a reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:141
msgid "When the panel is right, the reviewer clicks :guilabel:`Approve the Panel`. That is the moment the invitations go out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:144
msgid "The nomination form refuses, with a message saying why: nominating yourself; the same person twice in two capacities; somebody from another company; somebody as a *direct report* who does not report to the employee; a role this round does not ask for; too few or too many for a role; and — for an anonymous role — a number below the threshold, with the option of proposing none at all instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:151
msgid "The employee nominates through a form and never gains access to the panel record itself. Once an anonymous rater is accepted, they stop being listed even for the reviewer: from then on their answers exist only inside the pooled result. That is what makes the answers anonymous rather than merely unlabelled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:159
msgid "What a rater does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:162
msgid "Internal raters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:164
msgid "An internal rater gets a mail and a to-do, and finds the request at :menuselection:`Performance --> Reviews --> Feedback I Owe`. They answer the questions addressed to *Other raters*, and hand their feedback in when they are ready. Handing it in is final, and they are told so before confirming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:169
msgid "A rater who is not the right person to answer can decline, optionally saying why, and will not be asked about that review again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:173
msgid "Outside raters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:175
msgid "Somebody with no account gets a single-purpose link that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:177
msgid "carries a token that is **never stored** — only a fingerprint of it is kept, so a link can be reissued but never read back out of the database;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:179
msgid "**expires**, and says so in the invitation;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:180
msgid "resolves the review and the answerable questions from the token itself, never from anything the browser sends;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:182
msgid "is rate-limited, per link and per address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:184
msgid "An expired, unknown or already-used link shows a plain page explaining which of those it is and what to do — ask the person who invited you to send a new one — rather than an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:187
msgid "Outside raters can save their answers and come back to the same link to finish later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:190
msgid "What every rater is told"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:192
msgid "Before answering, every rater reads what will happen to their answers: whether the role they are answering in is anonymous, what the threshold is, that nothing at all is released below it, that written remarks are shuffled and separated from the question they were written under, and — for a non-anonymous role — that their answers are recorded under their name and how many of the questions are also shown to the person being reviewed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:199
msgid "That text is **generated from the settings of the round as they stand at that moment**, never shipped as a fixed sentence. A promise that outlives the configuration it was made under is not a promise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:206
msgid "What each person sees at the end"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:211
msgid "A :guilabel:`Multi-rater Feedback` page on the review, with one block per rater role: how many people answered, the average per question, and the written remarks pooled and shuffled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:214
msgid "A role that has not reached the threshold shows a short explanation instead — that nobody was asked in that group, that nobody has answered yet, or that fewer than the threshold have answered and therefore nothing is released, including the count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:218
msgid "Named roles behave differently: if a role was not promised anonymity, its answers appear as ordinary answers, attributed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:224
msgid "Whatever the reviewer decided to share, on the questions marked as shared, plus the released rating. Never an individual anonymous answer, and never the panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:228
msgid "HR officers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/multi_rater.rst:230
msgid "Everything the reviewer sees. An officer can read an individual non-anonymous answer; an anonymous one is excluded for them too."
msgstr ""

