#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:3
#: ../../content/applications/hr/salary/reconciliation.rst:109
#: ../../content/applications/hr/time_off/reporting.rst:3
msgid "Reporting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:5
msgid "Everything in this section reports on records the reader is already allowed to read. There is no reporting view that widens access: a reviewer's pivot table covers their own team, an officer's covers their companies, and an employee has no reporting menu at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:9
msgid "The reporting menu sits at :menuselection:`Performance --> Reporting` and is visible from the :guilabel:`Reviewer` access level up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:15
msgid "The cycle dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:17
msgid ":menuselection:`Performance --> Cycles --> Cycle Dashboard` opens a pivot and graph of reviews grouped by cycle and by status. It answers the question a cycle owner asks every morning: where is this wave stuck, and with whom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:21
msgid "Group it by :guilabel:`Reviewer` to find the manager with nine unstarted assessments, or by :guilabel:`Department` to see whether a whole area is behind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:24
msgid "Each cycle also reports on itself: :guilabel:`Reviews` and :guilabel:`Completed` smart buttons, a completion percentage in the cycle list, and a :guilabel:`Reviews` page listing every review with its employee, reviewers, due date, status and sign-off state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:31
msgid "Tracking completion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:33
msgid "The review list itself is the tracking tool. The search view carries the filters that matter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:36
msgid "What it brings up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:38
msgid ":guilabel:`To Do by Me`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:38
msgid "Reviews waiting for something from you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:40
msgid ":guilabel:`Open`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:40
msgid "Everything not yet closed or cancelled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:42
msgid ":guilabel:`Late`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:42
msgid "Past the due date and not finished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:44
msgid ":guilabel:`Waiting for Sign-off`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:44
msgid "Shared with the employee, still unsigned. The usual bottleneck of a cycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:47
msgid ":guilabel:`Disagreed`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:47
msgid "Signed off with a written disagreement. Read these; they are the most useful feedback the process produces about itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:51
msgid ":guilabel:`Past its Retention Date`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:51
msgid "Candidates for the purge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:55
msgid "Group by :guilabel:`Cycle`, :guilabel:`Reviewer`, :guilabel:`Department`, :guilabel:`Status`, :guilabel:`Sign-off` or :guilabel:`Due Date`. The Kanban view grouped by status gives the same picture as a board, and the calendar on the due date shows the shape of the coming fortnight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:60
msgid ":guilabel:`Waiting for Sign-off` combined with a group by reviewer is usually the most useful single view during a cycle. It separates \"the manager has not written it\" from \"the employee has not read it\", which need completely different chasing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:67
msgid "Scores and rating analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:69
msgid ":menuselection:`Performance --> Reporting --> Ratings` opens the confidential assessments as a list, graph and pivot: the proposed rating, the final rating, the self, manager and composite scores, the potential and the flight risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:81
msgid "Use it for the questions a single review cannot answer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:83
msgid "**Distribution.** How many people ended at each level, per department and per reviewer. Set a :guilabel:`Target Share (%)` on your scale levels and you have something to compare against — advisory guidance, never enforced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:86
msgid "**Reviewer effect.** Two managers of comparable teams whose average ratings differ by a whole level are worth a conversation before the next calibration round, not after it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:88
msgid "**Self versus manager.** A large systematic gap between the self-assessment score and the manager score, in either direction, usually says something about how expectations are being communicated rather than about the people."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:91
msgid "**Calibration.** The filter :guilabel:`Calibrated` shows where a final rating was moved away from what the reviewer proposed; each of those carries the written reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/hr/performance/reporting.rst:95
